the target language is: lps.

% Inform's "IQ Test" (Goal-Seeking Characters), in Logical English. See iqtest.lps.
% The English is the world and the rules; iqtest.lps, the companion, holds the
% narration table that turns the trace into prose.

the maximum time is 18.

the events are:
    the command is to open *a thing*; known as cmd_open.
    the command is to take *a thing*; known as cmd_take.
    the command is to eat *a thing*; known as cmd_eat.
    *a person* is asked to get *a thing*; known as ask_get.
    *a person* is asked to give *a thing* to *a second person*; known as ask_give.
    *a person* gets *a thing*; known as get.
    *a person* opens up *a thing*; known as open_up.
    *a person* tries to open *a thing*; known as try_open.
    *a person* tries to take *a thing*; known as try_take.

the actions are:
    *a person* opens *a thing*; known as open.
    *a person* unlocks *a thing* with *a key*; known as unlock.
    *a person* takes *a thing*; known as take.
    *a person* gives *a thing* to *a second person*; known as give.
    *a person* eats *a thing*; known as eat.
    *a note* is said about *a thing*; known as say.
    opening *a thing* is refused for *a person*; known as refuse_open.
    taking *a thing* is refused for *a person*; known as refuse_take.

the fluents are:
    *a thing* is in *a place*; known as in.
    *a person* carries *a thing*; known as carries.
    *a thing* is closed; known as closed.
    *a thing* is locked; known as locked.
    *a thing* is eaten; known as eaten.
    *a person* can reach *a thing*; known as reachable.

the templates are:
    the key of *a thing* is *a key*.
    *a thing* is edible.

the knowledge base iq test includes:

% Inform's assertions
initially ogg is in shop
    and player is in shop
    and case is in shop
    and donuts is in case
    and case is closed
    and case is locked
    and ogg carries key.

the key of case is key.
donuts is edible.

% a sliver of the Standard Rules: what an actor can reach
a person can reach a thing at a time if
    the person is in a place at the time
    and the thing is in the place at the time.

a person can reach a thing at a time if
    the person is in a place at the time
    and a container is in the place at the time
    and the thing is in the container at the time
    and it is not the case that the container is closed at the time.

a person can reach a thing at a time if
    the person carries the thing at the time.

% causal laws: Inform's carry-out rules
when a person unlocks a thing with a key
then it is not the case that the thing is locked.

when a person opens a thing
then it is not the case that the thing is closed.

when a person takes a thing
then the person carries the thing.

when a person takes a thing
then it is not the case that the thing is in a place.

when a person gives a thing to a second person
then it is not the case that the person carries the thing.

when a person gives a thing to a second person
then the second person carries the thing.

when a person eats a thing
then it is not the case that the person carries the thing.

when a person eats a thing
then the thing is eaten.

% preconditions: Inform's check rules, without their messages
it must not be true that
    a person opens a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is locked at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person opens a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is closed at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person unlocks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the key at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person takes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person eats a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the thing at the first time.

% the player's commands — the `instead` idiom: the message is one rule, the
% action is another, and each carries the condition that decides it
if the command is to open a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to open the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to take a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to take the thing from the second time to a third time.

% the `try` idiom: a command is not an obligation. The action, or else a
% refusal — and the refusal is narrated by asking the engine why not.
a person tries to open a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person opens the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to open a thing from a first time to a second time if
    opening the thing is refused for the person from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to take a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person takes the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to take a thing from a first time to a second time if
    taking the thing is refused for the person from the first time to the second time.

if the command is to eat a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is edible
then player eats the thing from the second time to a third time.

% "og, get donuts" — the goal-seeking character, as a composite event
if a person is asked to get a thing from a first time to a second time
then the person gets the thing from the second time to a third time.

if a person is asked to give a thing to a second person from a first time to a second time
    and the person carries the thing at the second time
then the person gives the thing to the second person from the second time to a third time.

a person gets a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person can reach the thing at the first time
    and the person takes the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person gets a thing from a first time to a third time if
    the thing is in a container at the first time
    and the container is closed at the first time
    and the person opens up the container from the first time to a second time
    and the person takes the thing from the second time to the third time.

a person opens up a thing from a first time to a second time if
    it is not the case that the thing is locked at the first time
    and the person opens the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person opens up a thing from a first time to a third time if
    the thing is locked at the first time
    and the key of the thing is a key
    and the person carries the key at the first time
    and the person unlocks the thing with the key from the first time to a second time
    and the person opens the thing from the second time to the third time.

scenario one is:
    the command is to open case from 1 to 2.
    the command is to take donuts from 4 to 5.
    ogg is asked to get donuts from 7 to 8.
    ogg is asked to give donuts to player from 13 to 14.
    the command is to eat donuts from 16 to 17.
